<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Cross-round universal-restriction propagation in the individual saturation.
  The individual saturation processes the ABox in rounds; a role partner in
  another round is replaced by a representative proxy. The consequence here is
  carried by a normalised existential GCI that becomes a universal restriction
  on the inverse role:

    r(a,b), s(b,c), A2(a), A1(c)
    SubClassOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(s, A1), B1)                  -> b : B1
    SubClassOf(ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(r, B1), A2), D1)
                                                                 -> a : exists r.B1, a : D1
    ClassAssertion(ObjectComplementOf(D1), a)                    -> contradiction

  a is an instance of D1 only through its role successor b's derived type B1.
  If b lands in a different saturation round than a (forced here by the small
  saturation batch system config), the universal restriction cannot be
  propagated to the real a inside the saturation, so a's type D1 is missed and
  the ontology is wrongly reported consistent. With the cross-round universal
  propagation fix the completion materialises the neighbour and derives D1, so
  not-D1(a) clashes and the ontology is inconsistent.

  Run with the small-saturation-batch system config so the split is forced on
  this tiny ontology (kt:usesTestSystemConfig). Without the fix this test is
  reported consistent; with the fix it is inconsistent.
-->
<Ontology xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" ontologyIRI="http://konclude.test/abox/cross-round-universal-propagation">
  <Declaration><ObjectProperty IRI="#r"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><ObjectProperty IRI="#s"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><Class IRI="#A1"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><Class IRI="#A2"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><Class IRI="#B1"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><Class IRI="#D1"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><NamedIndividual IRI="#a"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><NamedIndividual IRI="#b"/></Declaration>
  <Declaration><NamedIndividual IRI="#c"/></Declaration>
  <SubClassOf>
    <ObjectSomeValuesFrom><ObjectProperty IRI="#s"/><Class IRI="#A1"/></ObjectSomeValuesFrom>
    <Class IRI="#B1"/>
  </SubClassOf>
  <SubClassOf>
    <ObjectIntersectionOf>
      <ObjectSomeValuesFrom><ObjectProperty IRI="#r"/><Class IRI="#B1"/></ObjectSomeValuesFrom>
      <Class IRI="#A2"/>
    </ObjectIntersectionOf>
    <Class IRI="#D1"/>
  </SubClassOf>
  <ObjectPropertyAssertion><ObjectProperty IRI="#r"/><NamedIndividual IRI="#a"/><NamedIndividual IRI="#b"/></ObjectPropertyAssertion>
  <ObjectPropertyAssertion><ObjectProperty IRI="#s"/><NamedIndividual IRI="#b"/><NamedIndividual IRI="#c"/></ObjectPropertyAssertion>
  <ClassAssertion><Class IRI="#A2"/><NamedIndividual IRI="#a"/></ClassAssertion>
  <ClassAssertion><Class IRI="#A1"/><NamedIndividual IRI="#c"/></ClassAssertion>
  <ClassAssertion><ObjectComplementOf><Class IRI="#D1"/></ObjectComplementOf><NamedIndividual IRI="#a"/></ClassAssertion>
</Ontology>
